{
  "mn132:0.1": "Middle Discourses 132 ",
  "mn132:0.2": "Ānanda and One Fine Night ",
  "mn132:1.1": "So I have heard. ",
  "mn132:1.2": "At one time the Buddha was staying near Sāvatthī in Jeta’s Grove, Anāthapiṇḍika’s monastery. ",
  "mn132:2.1": "Now at that time Venerable Ānanda was educating, encouraging, firing up, and inspiring the mendicants in the assembly hall with a Dhamma talk on the topic of the summary recital and the analysis of the one who has one fine night. ",
  "mn132:2.2": "Then in the late afternoon, the Buddha came out of retreat, went to the assembly hall, where he sat down on the seat spread out, ",
  "mn132:2.3": "and addressed the mendicants: ",
  "mn132:2.4": "“Who was inspiring the mendicants with a talk on the summary recital and the analysis of the one who has one fine night?” ",
  "mn132:2.5": "“It was Venerable Ānanda, sir.” ",
  "mn132:2.6": "Then the Buddha said to Venerable Ānanda, ",
  "mn132:2.7": "“But in what way were you inspiring the mendicants with a talk on the summary recital and the analysis of the one who has one fine night?” ",
  "mn132:3.1": "“I was doing so in this way, sir,” replied Ānanda. ",
  "mn132:3.2": "“Don’t run back to the past, ",
  "mn132:3.3": "don’t anticipate the future. ",
  "mn132:3.4": "What’s past is left behind, ",
  "mn132:3.5": "the future has not arrived; ",
  "mn132:3.6": "and any present phenomenon ",
  "mn132:3.7": "you clearly discern in every case. ",
  "mn132:3.8": "The unfaltering, the unshak